# Snow and ash on the grass (grass.gdshader, slice 4), where they can lie on it.
# What settles on a blade is masked by what its ground can hold (SkyGround),
# as on the ground itself, so this is shot where a snowy and an ashen landscape
# meet grass: on seed 12 the snowfield meets the grey orchards' turf and the
# burning meets the sulphur jungle's. Each weather beside a dry frame of the
# same place and hour, over the shoulder.
#   tools/tour.sh tours/foliage_snow_ash.tour --seed=12
hour 11
coast calm
place snowfield-grey_orchards
ground grass
hold shoulder_peek
await shoulder 3
weather clear:0:wind=0.5
wait 3.0
shot 01-orchard-grass-by-the-snowfield-dry with border:snowfield-grey_orchards
weather snow:1:wind=0.5
wait 4.0
shot 02-orchard-grass-by-the-snowfield-snow with border:snowfield-grey_orchards
place burning-sulphur_jungle
ground grass
weather clear:0:wind=0.5
wait 3.0
shot 03-jungle-grass-by-the-burning-dry with border:burning-sulphur_jungle
weather ash:1:wind=0.5
wait 4.0
shot 04-jungle-grass-by-the-burning-ash with border:burning-sulphur_jungle
release shoulder_peek
weather rules
